course: dictionary
lesson: 12764
title: Earmarks: setting money aside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An earmark is a word with more than one meaning, so the clues around it matter. Read the words near it and ask what would fit here. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The council earmarked money for a new park.» The clue is money for a park. To earmark means to set something aside for a special purpose, so the council has put that money to one side for the park and nothing else.
explain: «The senator put an earmark in the bill to pay for a bridge in his home town.» In a government budget, an earmark is money set aside for a politician's favourite local project. Some people call it pork and say it is a waste of money, so the clues show it is a word people argue about.
explain: «The farmer's sheep had a mark on one ear.» Here earmark has its literal meaning: a mark on an animal's ear. The context tells you which meaning is the right one.
fact: Earmark can be a noun (an earmark) or a verb (to earmark, earmarks, earmarked).
fact: As a verb, «earmark» means to set money or something aside for a purpose.
fact: In US politics, an earmark is money in a budget for a politician's favourite local projects, often criticised as waste.
fact: In US politics, «earmarks» is a softer word for «pork», which means spending to win votes.
fact: Literally, an earmark is a mark on an animal's ear.
exercise: «The school earmarked money for new computers.» What does earmarked mean? | *Set aside for a purpose | Spent all at once on sweets | Lost in the post | Argued about in a meeting
exercise: The farmer checked the earmark on the lamb's ear to see whose it was. What is an earmark here? | A kind of sheep dog | *A mark on an animal's ear | A small present for a friend | A sum of money in a budget
exercise: Which word is a softer way to say «pork» in US politics? | Garden | Guitar | Tunnel | *Earmark
test: «The senator's earmark paid for a new road in his state, and many people said it was a waste.» What does earmark mean in this sentence? | *Money in a budget for a politician's favourite local project | A loud cheer at a vote | A mark on a horse's ear | A type of road sign
test: «Mum earmarked her savings for a summer holiday.» What does earmarked mean? | *Set it aside for a special purpose | Gave it to the bank as a prize | Lost it on the way home | Spent it all straight away
exam: Maya reads, «The council earmarked money for the library.» Which sentence explains the meaning of earmarked best? | *It set the money aside for the library | It threw the money away on a bad idea | It counted all the money in the town | It put a mark on the library's ear
